---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Steps from '../components/Steps.astro';
import Generator from '../components/Generator';
import { config, workstreams, withBase } from '../lib/site';
import { RESERVED_WORDS, NAME_MAX, DESC_MAX, BODY_MAX_LINES } from '../lib/skill-rules';
import { DETAIL_KEYS } from '../../scripts/lib/skill-details.mjs';

const steps = [
  { title: 'Spot a task you repeat', body: 'If you keep explaining the same job to Claude, it is a good candidate.' },
  { title: 'Draft it here or with Claude', body: 'Use the generator below, or ask Claude to draft and test it with skill-creator. The generator checks it as you type.' },
  { title: 'Add a made-up example', body: 'Include a small sample with invented names and figures so others can see it work.' },
  { title: 'Share it', body: 'Send it to the maintainers, or suggest the idea on the roadmap first. It is reviewed before it joins the library.' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Contribute"
  current="contribute"
  description="Turn a task the team repeats into a skill. Draft it with the generator, then share it for review."
>
  <PageHead title="Contribute" lede="Turn a task the team repeats into a skill everyone can use. Draft it here, then share it for review." />

  <section aria-labelledby="h-add">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="h-add">Adding a skill, in four steps</h2>
      <p class="sec-intro">You do not need to be a developer. The generator below writes the starting file for you.</p>
      <Steps items={steps} columns={4} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="h-ways">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="h-ways">Two ways to draft a skill</h2>
      <p class="sec-intro">Use either one, or both. Whichever you start with, finish in the generator so the site details are filled in.</p>
      <div class="ways">
        <div class="way">
          <h3>The generator on this page</h3>
          <p>Fill in the form and it writes <code>SKILL.md</code> for you, checked against the house rules as you type. It runs in your browser and sends nothing anywhere.</p>
          <p class="dt">Best for a first draft, or when you want the rules checked as you go.</p>
          <p><a href="#h-gen">Go to the generator</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="way">
          <h3>Draft and test it with Claude</h3>
          <p>
            Anthropic publishes a skill called <strong>skill-creator</strong>. Ask Claude to use it and it will draft the skill, write a few test prompts, run them <em>with and without</em> your skill, show you the results, and help you revise until it works. It can also tune the description so Claude picks the skill up at the right moment.
          </p>
          <p class="dt">Best when you want to see whether the skill really changes Claude's answers before you share it.</p>
          <p class="way-h">In Claude Code</p>
          <div class="cmd cmd-sm">
            <pre tabindex="0">/plugin marketplace add anthropics/skills
/plugin install example-skills@anthropic-agent-skills</pre>
          </div>
          <p class="dt">
            Then ask: <q>Use skill-creator to help me turn this job into a skill.</q> skill-creator is part of the <code>example-skills</code> plugin in <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/skills" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Anthropic's skills repository</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="way-h">In claude.ai</p>
          <p class="dt">
            Anthropic lists the example skills as available on paid plans. Skills need code execution to be switched on, and you turn them on under <strong>Customize &gt; Skills</strong>. The menu wording may differ in the app.
          </p>
          <p class="way-h">Try a finished draft day to day</p>
          <p class="dt">Copy the skill's folder into <code>~/.claude/skills/</code> and type its name with a slash.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="body ways-end">
        <strong>Before you share it,</strong> make sure its <code>SKILL.md</code> has the <code>metadata</code> block the generator below writes: fill in "Details for the Skills library" and copy the result into your file. The site needs <code>{DETAIL_KEYS.workstream}</code>, <code>{DETAIL_KEYS.tagline}</code>, <code>{DETAIL_KEYS.give}</code> and <code>{DETAIL_KEYS.get}</code> to build the skill's tile and page, and it will not publish a skill that is missing them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="h-gen">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="h-gen">Skill generator</h2>
      <p class="sec-intro">It checks your skill against the house rules as you type. It runs in your browser and sends nothing anywhere.</p>
      <Generator client:load ticketPrefix={config.ticketPrefix} fictionalName={config.fictionalName} workstreams={workstreams} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="h-rules">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="h-rules">The rules in full</h2>
      <p class="sec-intro">The generator checks most of these for you. They are here so you can see why.</p>

      <details class="fold">
        <summary>What is inside a skill</summary>
        <pre class="tree">skills/a-skill/
  SKILL.md     <em>short body: when to use it, and the recipe</em>
  references/  <em>detail Claude loads only when needed</em>
  scripts/     <em>deterministic helpers for the exact steps</em>
examples/a-skill/
               <em>made-up samples so others can see it work</em></pre>
      </details>
      <details class="fold">
        <summary>House rules</summary>
        <p>
          Keep the SKILL.md body to roughly 150 to 200 lines and push detail into references. Never copy or paraphrase other skills' code or prose. Use only the made-up bank in anything committed ({config.fictionalName}, ticket prefix {config.ticketPrefix}-). Real client files stay in a local, ignored folder.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="fold">
        <summary>Limits from the Agent Skills specification</summary>
        <p>
          The name is 1 to {NAME_MAX} characters: lowercase letters, numbers and single hyphens, with no hyphen at either end. It must match the folder name and can't contain {RESERVED_WORDS.map((w) => `"${w}"`).join(' or ')} or any XML tags. The description is 1 to {DESC_MAX} characters, can't contain XML tags, and should say what the skill does and when to use it. Keep the whole SKILL.md under {BODY_MAX_LINES} lines. Claude Code also skips a skill folder named "synced".
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="fold">
        <summary>Shipping it and trying it locally</summary>
        <p>
          Work on a branch, add the skill folder and made-up samples, add a row to the README skills table, commit with a sign-off and open a pull request. Pull requests come from collaborators only. To try a skill before it merges, copy its folder into your personal skills folder (<code>~/.claude/skills/</code>) and type its name with a slash.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="h-idea">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="h-idea">Not ready to write one?</h2>
      <p class="sec-intro">Suggest the idea on the roadmap, and someone on the team can pick it up.</p>
      <a class="btn pri" href={withBase('/roadmap/')}>Go to the roadmap</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
